  "purpose": "Measure family-level suppression under normalized complete-command MAP versus marginal family argmax, using frozen causal upstream features. Distinguish this from weak type beliefs and unchanged integer-mode errors.",
  "models": [
    "L02",
    "U01"
  ],
  "sampling": "All original DEV rows; augmented and natural-membership TRAIN reported separately. Same cached augmented-cadence filtering; not natural cadence.",
  "outputs": "Only marginal family log probabilities/type-argmax diagnostics; existing complete commands stay unchanged. No new complete-predictor variant selected or scored.",
  "interpretation": "Joint MAP correctly discounts uncertain conditional arguments. A difference from type argmax is not objective/decoder inconsistency. Relations to omitted own priority channels are descriptive, not causal attribution. No fitting.",
